8 0 obj
<< /Length 1463 >>
stream
BT 0.45 g /F2 12 Tf 32 443.95 Td (Chapter 3) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 28 Tf 32 407.55 Td (Contextual Retrieval) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 367.43 Td (A retrieval system is only as good as the pieces of text it finds. When documents) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 341.43 Td (are split into chunks, the link to the whole document is often lost: a sentence like) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 315.43 Td (\223Revenue grew by 3 percent in the second quarter\224 names neither the company nor) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 289.43 Td (the year.) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 251.43 Td (Contextual retrieval puts a short, model-written description in front of every chunk) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 225.43 Td (before it is embedded, placing it within the whole document. The same description) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 199.43 Td (goes into the BM25 index, so lexical and semantic search gain from the same extra) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 173.43 Td (context.) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 135.43 Td (The extra effort comes once, at indexing time, and prompt caching lowers it) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 109.43 Td (considerably. The length of the added context still matters: too short and it does not) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 83.43 Td (place the chunk, too long and it dilutes the embedding.) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 45.43 Td (In practice it pays to compare on a small test set before the whole collection is) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 19.43 Td (indexed again.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
