10 0 obj
<< /Length 1085 >>
stream
BT 0 g /F1 22 Tf 32 434.57 Td (Writing the context) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 399.43 Td (For every chunk the model gets two inputs: the full document and the single chunk.) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 373.43 Td (The instruction is, in essence, to describe in one or two sentences where this section) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 347.43 Td (sits in the document and what it is about. Nothing more is needed.) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 309.43 Td (Because the document stays the same for all of its chunks, it is ideal for prompt) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 283.43 Td (caching. The document is loaded into the cache once; every further call only pays) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 257.43 Td (for the short chunk and the answer. For long manuals the cost drops to a fraction.) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 219.43 Td (The generated context is put in front of the chunk, and only this combined text is) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 193.43 Td (embedded and written to the BM25 index. The original chunk is kept for display in) Tj ET
BT 0 g /F1 16.5 Tf 32 167.43 Td (the search result.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Type /Page /Parent 2 0 R /MediaBox [0 0 620 484] /Resources << /Font << /F1 3 0 R /F2 4 0 R >> >> /Contents 10 0 R >>
